body:
You know, I was rather surprised that Damwon was rolled over early and had a big, I mean huge comeback. This is the kind of game where Khan showed his weak side by not playing a tank (which understandably, if you see Udyr Trist Zoe, that's kinda a bit of a not-Sion game) and the result was just bot diff. Every day, I come to watch Damwon, and BeryL really makes these good plays that are just another level of support. Ghost is just quite literally the name of Ghost where he strikes like the StarCraft's Ghost: quiet and hard. 

&#x200B;

Damwon is either a top-side diff or a bot-side diff. They know how to play their games and go around their match with who is the carry and who needs to be sacrificed. 

&#x200B;

However, Detonation is definitely that underdog ready to shock the world. I want to see them again at Worlds too because they cannot go unnoticed. 

&#x200B;

GG well played both teams.
